    <p class="lp-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="lp-h1">About Us</h1>

    <p>Welcome to <a href="https://bodyshapecalculator.net/">BodyShapeCalculator.net</a>, your trusted destination for precision-based body analysis.</p>

    <p>We built this site on a simple idea: generic health metrics like BMI treat every body the same, when in reality everyone is built differently. Our mission is to move past one-size-fits-all numbers and give you insights based on your own proportions — the actual relationship between your bust, waist, high hip and hip measurements, not just your height and weight.</p>

    <h2>What We Offer</h2>
    <p>Our Body Type Calculator uses a documented, seven-shape classification system — drawn from published clothing-science research — to analyze your measurements and identify your specific body shape, whether that's Hourglass, Pear, Apple, Inverted Triangle, Rectangle, or one of their less-common variants. Alongside your shape result, we also calculate your Waist-to-Hip Ratio (WHR) and Waist-to-Height Ratio (WHtR), two measures researchers use to understand fat distribution and related health context — clearly separated from the styling side of things, so you always know which is which.</p>

    <div class="lp-card">
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">Every calculator on this site runs entirely in your browser. We don't collect, store, or transmit the measurements you enter — see our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for the full details.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Who We're For</h2>
    <p>Whether you're refining your personal style, curious about the numbers behind waist-to-hip ratio, or simply want to understand your own proportions better, our tools are built for both men and women, worldwide, and are always free to use.</p>

    <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
    <p>We're committed to accuracy, transparency, and a genuinely useful experience — not just another calculator that spits out a label with no context. That's why every result on this site comes with the exact formula behind it, sourced explanations, and practical guidance you can actually use.</p>

    <p>Have a question or a suggestion? We'd love to hear from you on our <a href="/contact-us/">Contact page</a>.</p>
